        "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9f5cb06a8a6e99d7447d60db1d503e05167950da.001.1",
        "event": "Heat Advisory",
        "headline": "Heat Advisory issued August 10 at 5:00AM AKDT until August 10 at 8:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Temperatures in the middle to upper 70s expected.\n\n* WHERE...Lower Matanuska Valley\n\n* WHEN...Until 8 PM AKDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Individuals not accustomed to these temperatures may\nexperience heat related illnesses.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Similar to what was observed yesterday\n(Sunday) afternoon, the warmest forecast temperatures in the lower\nMatanuska Valley will likely occur west of Wasilla, including\nHouston and Big Lake.",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Expected",
        "sender": "NWS Anchorage AK",
        "effective": "2026-08-10T05:00:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-08-10T20:00:00-08:00",
        "areas": "Lower Matanuska Valley",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Execute",
        "instruction": "Drink plenty of fluids and check up on elderly and vulnerable\nrelatives and neighbors.\n\nTake extra precautions when working in the sun. Wear sunscreen and\nlightweight, loose fitting clothing. Try to limit strenuous\nactivities to early morning or evening. Take action when you see\nsymptoms of heat exh",
        "lat": null,
        "lng": null
      },
      {
        "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eb0fef687605f13ac4d19148a5c682630426aec9.001.1",
        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued August 9 at 12:11PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "Unusually warm temperatures are likely through Monday early\nevening. The warmest temperatures will occur during the afternoon\ninto early evening, today and Monday.\n\nHigh temperatures across the Anchorage Bowl and lower Hillside\nwill be in the low to mid 70s. Expect warmer temperatures inland\nwith cooler temperatures along the coast. The overnight low will\nbe in the 50s.\n\nTake extra precautions when working in the sun. Wear sunscreen\nand lightweight, loose fitting clothing. Try to limit strenuous",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Observed",
        "urgency": "Expected",
        "sender": "NWS Anchorage AK",
        "effective": "2026-08-09T12:11:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-08-10T06:00:00-08:00",
